The task’s meaningful domain is positive integers: zero and negatives have no finite list of positive prime factors whose product equals the input, while `1` validly maps to the empty list. I’m implementing unbounded trial division over `n >= 1`; the proof invariant will retain a symbolic remaining integer and divisor, so it covers all positive sizes rather than bounded examples.
